      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/helena_valley_west_central_montana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After gold mining declined in the late 19th century, homesteading and agriculture expanded in Helena Valley, helped by the 1862 Homestead Act and the 1883 Northern Pacific Railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/helena_valley_west_central_montana",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Helena’s historic downtown, just a couple of miles from West Central, features Last Chance Road—a pedestrian mall lined with brick buildings that once housed Main Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://discoveringmontana.com/towns/helena-valley-west-central/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Montana Historical Society museum near West Central offers extensive exhibits on wildlife, Lewis and Clark, Native American culture, and paleontology.",
